{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"- **Application:** File an exemptive application with the SEC explaining the requested relief, relevant facts, legal basis, and proposed conditions. Staff reviews it and may require amendments.\n- **Notice:** The SEC publishes notice of the proposed relief, allowing interested persons to request a hearing—ordinarily with at least 25 days’ notice before an order.\n- **Order:** If no hearing is required and the SEC approves, it issues an order granting relief subject to its conditions.\n\n**Rule 0-5 expedited review** is available for properly designated applications substantially identical to two applications granted within the preceding three years, with required comparison materials.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Its 45-calendar-day clock targets **notice, not approval**. It pauses for staff comments and resumes 14 days after a responsive amendment. Staff may determine the application is ineligible or requires further consideration. It is not a guaranteed total approval period."}}
